    "Stage 3's index wait polled its largest library (about 200 vectors), which Cosmos reads whole at that size, so 'stops scanning' never applied; it timed out after 30 minutes and the probes were measured after the settle period. Probe libraries reported their sharded index as before.",
    "The new-library lag test added a 1,500-passage library after stage 2; the container at stage 3 therefore held 1,014 libraries and 244,773 passages, as the unscoped control's documents-read figure shows.",
    "Everything ran on one physical partition of a serverless account. Write charge was about 92 RU per passage: these passages are single abstracts, shorter than the canary's chunks (144 RU, E10).",
    "The canary passed on the disposable database before loading (15.2 RU median, recall 1.0, hybrid ranking)."
